VERDICT: PARTIAL — these are the committed round-1 panes (a single sample); the authoritative scrape reliability is the multi-round aggregate in tmux.log. On these panes whole-line parsing and column-aware parsing differ (the sidebar shares rows, so whole-line can miss or match the wrong column), and long replies are cut to the visible screen (alt-screen, no tmux scrollback). Separately, tmux.log shows the old whole-line checker also false-positives mid-turn on the sidebar auto-title before any reply exists. Net: pane scraping is lossy and can false-positive; the HTTP API supersedes it.
